From: Godot native media integration
Subject: [PATCH] avformat/hls: classify HTTPS for application-owned AVIO

HLS validates the URL's protocol name before invoking the application io_open
callback. A build without a builtin TLS backend cannot recognize HTTPS here,
even when the application provides HTTPS through custom AVIO. Classify plain
HTTPS URLs on the custom-IO path and retain all existing protocol checks and
the application's io_open callback. This adds no socket or TLS implementation.

Applies to FFmpeg n9.0.2, 946fcce07b6dcd0331c8cc609192aeff5e1924f8.

--- a/libavformat/hls.c
+++ b/libavformat/hls.c
@@ -696,6 +696,12 @@ static int open_url(AVFormatContext *s, AVIOContext **pb, const char *url,
             proto_name = avio_find_protocol_name(url + 5);
     }
 
+    /* Application-owned AVIO can provide HTTPS without a builtin TLS backend.
+     * This only classifies the URL; io_open still owns opening/validation. */
+    if (!proto_name && (s->flags & AVFMT_FLAG_CUSTOM_IO) &&
+        av_strstart(url, "https://", NULL))
+        proto_name = "https";
+
     if (!proto_name)
         proto_name = avio_find_protocol_name(url);
 
